# =============================================================================
# WAKA local-dev environment template
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FOR LOCAL DEVELOPMENT, COPY THIS TO `.env.local`:
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# That is the file `scripts/dev-local.sh` reads, and the only one it reads.
# This header said `.env` until 2026-08-28, which sent every new developer to
# a file `pnpm dev:local` does not open — it warns and starts anyway, so the
# stack came up with no database and failed later, somewhere else.
#
# DO NOT commit the populated file. `.env.local` is enough on its own for all
# of local development — `pnpm dev:local`, `tools/seed-demo.ts`, drizzle-kit
# (`drizzle.config.ts` loads it OVER `.env`), and `packages/api/test/setup.ts`
# (reads `.env` first, then lets `.env.local` override).
#
# A repo-root `.env` is only for one-off operator commands such as
# `pnpm sst secret set`. Nothing in the local loop requires it.
#
# Then run the matching `pnpm sst secret set ...` commands shown in README.md
# so the SST stack picks the values up at runtime. At Lambda runtime, secrets
# come from SST, not from any file. See sst.config.ts.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used by:
#   - the Hono API (process.env.DB_CONNECTION_URL ?? process.env.DATABASE_URL)
#   - the classifier queue worker
#   - drizzle-kit (migrations/studio)
# Mirror as DATABASE_URL only if a tool insists on that name; the codebase
# prefers DB_CONNECTION_URL.
#
# LOCAL — `docker compose up -d --wait` serves exactly this, and any
# Postgres 16 does too: nothing here needs an extension, because embeddings
# are `jsonb` (see `packages/api/src/db/schema-embeddings.ts`). Keep this line
# uncommented for local work. The database-backed API suite wants a separate
# `waka_test`; see README, "A database".
DB_CONNECTION_URL=postgres://waka:waka@127.0.0.1:5432/waka
#
# DEPLOYED / SHARED — a pooled Neon URL with sslmode=require, for the stages
# and for `pnpm sst secret set DbConnectionUrl`.
# DB_CONNECTION_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST.neon.tech/DB?sslmode=require&channel_binding=require

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Random base64 strings, ≥ 32 bytes of entropy. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 48
AUTH_SECRET=replace-with-base64-random-32-bytes-or-more
JWT_SECRET=replace-with-base64-random-32-bytes-or-more

# Google OAuth 2.0 credentials. Provision in Google Cloud Console as described
# in docs/google-oauth-setup.md. The "authorized redirect URI" must include the
# `sst dev` API URL printed by `pnpm dev` plus `/api/auth/google/callback`.
AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=000000000000-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=GOCSPX-replace-with-google-client-secret

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AWS (used by `sst dev` and the smoke tests)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `sst dev` reads credentials via the standard AWS SDK chain. You can either:
#   (a) set the *_APP variables here and `export` them as AWS_REGION /
#       AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY in your shell, or
#   (b) run `aws configure --profile waka-dev` and `export AWS_PROFILE=waka-dev`.
# Region MUST match `AWS_REGION` in sst.config.ts (us-west-2 today) or
# presigned PUTs will 301-PermanentRedirect.
AWS_REGION_APP=us-west-2
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID_APP=AKIA-replace-with-iam-access-key
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY_APP=replace-with-iam-secret-access-key

# Optional: a pre-existing S3 bucket name if you want the smoke tests to point
# at it. Production uploads use the SST-provisioned `Attachments` bucket whose
# name is injected as ATTACHMENTS_BUCKET at runtime.
S3_AWS_BUCKET_NAME=replace-with-s3-bucket-name

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM (Gemini)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API key for Google AI Studio (https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey).
# Used by the classifier queue worker only — never sent to the browser.
GEMINI_API_KEY=replace-with-gemini-api-key

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional / debug
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Explicit opt-in for conversation replies. Keep off until this environment is
# migrated and its provider/cost limits are verified. Never expose model keys.
WAKA_CONVERSATION_REPLIES=0
# DEBUG=true
# LOG_LEVEL=debug
# NODE_ENV=development
